{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - Security - Events - Okta Threat Suspected on an Authentication Request",
	"Description": "Okta marked an authentication request as threatSuspected. Unlike security.threat.detected this rides along on an ordinary authentication event, so it catches requests Okta was suspicious of but still processed.\n\nField: debugContext.debugData.threatSuspected == true\n\nReference(s):\n- https://help.okta.com/en-us/content/topics/security/threat-insight/okta-threatinsight-overview.htm\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "96ec1b96-3c45-5ee5-8426-1a17de7abcc6",
	"SearchReference": "279b1bd5-6265-5873-9abd-5a6ca2d5c959"
